  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "2sWLnrwDbFacV5YEJ+ZEjL0rMyI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:54:55.760Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The analytics engine's dimensional model is hierarchical (paths like `atlas/scopes/SUP/I/PHOENIX/`), and the documented way to work with it is **general first, then narrow**:\n\n> \"Looking at the dimension section in the filter options: to see available sub paths for the budget, leave the `select: \"atlas\"` and `lod` as 5. With `lod: 5` you'll be able to see the different paths available under your defined filter. Then, later, you can apply a more detailed path in the `select: \"atlas/...\"` path that will suit your needs.\"\n\n```json\n{ \"filter\": { \"dimensions\": [ { \"name\": \"budget\", \"select\": \"atlas\", \"lod\": 5 } ] } }\n```\n\nSo `lod` (level of detail) is an **exploration tool** as much as a rollup depth: a query is also how you discover the taxonomy. The same applies to the vocabulary itself \u2014 `analytics { metrics }` and `analytics { dimensions { name values { path label description icon } } }` are queries whose whole purpose is to tell you what you may filter on.\n\nTwo operational rules from the same page: **upper- and lower-case matter** for metric and granularity names, so a mistyped case returns nothing rather than erroring; and **fetch per specified path** if performance is a concern, rather than pulling a broad subtree.\n\nThe guidance on combining dimensions is judgement, not mechanism, and its useful half is the warning: combining dimensions adds depth, but \"avoid overly complex combinations that might lead to confusing or inconclusive results.\"\n\n## Provenance\n- `apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/04-WorkWithData/_06-Analytics Engine/best-practices.md` \u2014 GraphQL best practices (start general, case rules, fetch per path); Guidelines for selecting and combining dimensions\n- `apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/04-WorkWithData/_06-Analytics Engine/use-cases/maker.md` \u2014 Available metrics and Available dimensions queries\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:54:55.760Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:54:55.760Z"
    }
  },
